<header><p class="st-kicker">principality · Mesopotamia and Iran</p><h1 class="st-title">Muzaffarid dynasty</h1><p class="st-meta">1314 CE – 1393 CE (approx.) · capital Shiraz</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A Persian dynasty that ruled Fars, Kerman and central Iran after the Ilkhanate collapsed, remembered as the patrons, and sometimes the critics, of the poet Hafez.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>The Muzaffarids were a family of Arab descent who served the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/ilkhanate">Ilkhanate</a> as local officials. In 1319 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mubariz-al-din-muhammad">Mubariz al-Din Muhammad</a> defeated the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/atabegs-of-yazd">Atabegs of Yazd</a> and took the city. After the death of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ilkhan">Ilkhan</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/abu-said-bahadur-khan">Abu Sa'id</a> in 1335 he expanded rapidly, taking <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kerman">Kerman</a> in 1340 and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shiraz">Shiraz</a> from the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/injuid-dynasty">Injuid dynasty</a> in 1353.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mubariz-al-din-muhammad">Mubariz al-Din</a> was a stern ruler who closed taverns in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shiraz">Shiraz</a>, a mood <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hafez">Hafez</a> mocked in his verse; in 1358 his sons blinded and deposed him. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shah-shuja-muzaffarid">Shah Shuja</a> (1358 to 1384) presided over a brilliant court in Shiraz where Hafez wrote much of his poetry, though the family was torn by fratricidal wars. The dynasty ruled <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yazd">Yazd</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kerman">Kerman</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fars">Fars</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/isfahan">Isfahan</a> through princes of the house.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/timur">Timur's</a> invasions overwhelmed the divided family. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shah-mansur">Shah Mansur</a> defied him and was killed near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shiraz">Shiraz</a> in 1393, and Timur executed the remaining princes, incorporating their lands into the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/timurid-empire">Timurid Empire</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="principality, 1314 CE – 1393 CE (approx.)"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M20 74 H80 V60 H20 Z"/><path d="M20 60 Q35 46 50 60 Q65 46 80 60"/><circle cx="20" cy="54" r="3"/><circle cx="35" cy="48" r="3"/><circle cx="50" cy="44" r="3"/><circle cx="65" cy="48" r="3"/><circle cx="80" cy="54" r="3"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">principality</p><p class="st-emblem-region">Mesopotamia and Iran</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:85.85%;width:1.57%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1314 CE – 1393 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Century</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/14th-century">14th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>principality</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Shiraz</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Mubariz al-Din Muhammad, Shah Shuja, Shah Mansur</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Sunni Islam</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Persian</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/iran">Iran</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Muzaffarids</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1354&amp;focus=muzaffarid-dynasty" aria-label="Muzaffarid dynasty on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="6047 1096 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Muzaffarid dynasty lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M6367 1352L6416 1372M6367 1352L6400 1274M6367 1352L6367 1352M6367 1352L6134 1224M6367 1352L6582 1190"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M6416 1372h0M6400 1274h0M6367 1352h0M6134 1224h0M6582 1190h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M6367 1352h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M6367 1352h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Shiraz. <a href="/atlas?year=1354&amp;focus=muzaffarid-dynasty">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
